    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "## SUPERSEDED — USEFUL SECURITY CONTENT PORTED TO CURRENT MAIN\n\nThe stale 21-commit candidate is no longer the integration vehicle.\n\nFresh current-main repairs now incorporated its useful security boundaries through two narrow, freshly verified PRs:\n- #260 -> required SHERIFF secrets + immutable digest-pinned runtime images; exact-head `hq-validate`, `oss-security`, `sheriff-oss-validate`, and `sheriff-runtime-e2e` all SUCCESS before merge;\n- #261 -> terminal PASS evidence/run binding + execution-request identity binding; exact-head `hq-validate` and `oss-security` SUCCESS before merge.\n\nFresh main after #261 = `05cf881b175cec98030c4bba0efaf4870b91cd85`.\n\nThe old R30 goal to bind a live LESTER executor has separately been superseded by current-main `R03_RETIRED_FROM_AUTOMATION` and closure of #253/#110/#111; no live code executor is the safer current state.\n\nDisposition: close this stale PR unmerged as `SUPERSEDED BY #260 + #261 + CURRENT ROUTE RETIREMENT`. Preserve RED/GREEN history as evidence.",
